      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6cbcffd04b1785f747b6c|full_name}: This seems like a poor method of implementing that idea, one PC might stuggle with 10 good avatars, while another would be fine with 10 V.Poor avatars\n\nIf you want to implement quality scaling to performance, an api to get fps or cpu/gpu utilisation would be a far better option as it would consider the actual performance the user is getting, rather then what the world creater thinks they would get.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
